  m_Name: Ending_OtherPanda
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Ending
  endingTitle: Panda
  titleDA: 'Sammen Med Den Anden Panda '
  descriptionDA: "Pandaerne deler omr\xE5det. Bambussen er knap, og de holder sandsynligvis
    ikke sammen l\xE6nge endnu, Men mens de er sammen, har de en chance for at f\xE5
    unger. \n\nPandaer lever for det meste alene og m\xF8des kun kort om for\xE5ret
    for at parre sig. N\xE5r skoven bliver delt op, kan dyrene ikke n\xE5 hinanden,
    og bestanden bliver mere ensartet og mere s\xE5rbar. Sammenh\xE6ngende skov g\xF8r
    en forskel.\n\nN\xE5r du g\xE5r i zoo st\xF8tter du pandaerne, de er med i et
    avls program af China Wildlife Conservation Association som er del i at sikre
    pandaens langsigtede overlevelse. Hvis du skal k\xF8be bambus produkter kan du
    selv kigge efter FSC-m\xE6rkede produkter som garantere at vigtige levesteder
    ikke er blevet \xF8delagt. "
  titleEN: Together With The Other Panda
  descriptionEN: "The pandas share the area. Bamboo is scarce, so they probably won\u2019t
    stay together much longer. But for now, they have a chance of having cubs. \n\nPandas
    mostly live alone and only meet briefly in spring to mate. When forest is divided
    up, animals can\u2019t reach each other, and the population becomes more uniform
    and more vulnerable. Connected forest makes a difference.\n\nWhen you visit the
    zoo, you support the pandas. They are part of a breeding program run by the China
    Wildlife Conservation Association, which helps secure the panda\u2019s long-term
    survival. When buying bamboo products, look for the FSC label, which guarantees
    that important habitats haven\u2019t been destroyed. "
  endingImage: {fileID: 0}
